@startuml forkcast_sequence_log
title Forkcast - weigh and log with the app open
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam dpi 140
autonumber

participant "Active scale" as Scale
participant ScaleLink as Link
participant "ScaleAdapter\n(ESN00 or WSS)" as Adapter
participant ScaleManager as Manager
participant WeighSession as Session
participant Screens
participant Repositories as Repo
actor "Phone user" as User

Scale -> Link : measurement packets
Link -> Adapter : parse(bytes)
Adapter --> Manager : Reading(grams, stable)
Manager --> Session : reading from active scale\n(most recent if several on, FR-34)
Session -> Screens : placement: open Live weighing (Auto-open)\nand update grams (NFR-13)
User -> Screens : pick food (grams or servings)
alt scale disconnects before Log
  Link --> Session : disconnected
  Session --> Screens : show disconnected,\noffer typed grams
else stable reading, or grams typed
  Screens --> User : Log enabled (FR-40)
  User -> Screens : Log
  Screens -> Repo : insert entry + nutrient snapshot\n(one transaction, target 1 s, NFR-01)
  alt write fails
    Repo --> Screens : error (retried once)
    Screens --> User : show error, keep grams and food
  else written
    Repo --> Screens : entry id
    Screens --> User : Today and pinned goals update
  end
end
opt user closes without logging
  Screens --> User : ask, then discard (nothing saved)
end

legend bottom
  Typed grams, servings, and each item of a Weigh several session
  use the same Log transaction. Unknown nutrient values stay null;
  totals count them as 0 and mark the goal partial (FR-20, FR-72).
endlegend
@enduml
